38
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:43,290
莱纳德  我想问你好久  你穿多大的鞋子
Leonard, I've been meaning to ask you:what size shoe do you wear?

39
00:02:43,710 --> 00:02:44,750
怎么了
Why?

40
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:47,750
我在尝试对别人的生活感兴趣
I'm trying to take more of an interest in other people's lives.

41
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:52,380
那很好啊  我穿八号半的鞋
That's nice. I wear a size eight and a half.

42
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:54,220
脚好小啊
That's small.

43
00:02:56,890 --> 00:02:59,980
说说你这周末有没有什么安排吧
So, tell me, do you have any plans for the weekend?

44
00:03:00,230 --> 00:03:01,850
你会取笑我的答案吗
Are you gonna laugh at the answer?

45
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:04,440
除非你的答案是"去买婴儿鞋"
Only if the answer is "Shopping for baby shoes."

46
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:11,400
如果你真想知道 佩妮公司奖给她去水疗度假村度周末 她要带我去
If you must know,Penny won a spa weekend from work and she's taking me.

47
00:03:11,650 --> 00:03:13,490
这还真挺有趣呢
Oh, well you know, that is interesting.

48
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:15,910
忍不住想看你会感染哪些东西回家
I wonder what kind of infection you'll come home with.

49
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:19,410
我赌真菌感染
My money's on fungal.

50
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:25,000
女生们还在对面办女生之夜
They're still having girls' night across the hall.

51
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,500
那你来我这咱们办男生之夜啊
Oh, so, hang out with me and we'll have boys' night.

52
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:30,840
我们这年纪了  为什么不称呼为爷们之夜
At our age,why don't we call it man's night?

53
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:34,300
因为我们刚把零花钱都拿去买漫画了
Because we just spent our allowance on comic books.

54
00:03:38,930 --> 00:03:41,560
佩妮  你会别扭吗  就是你不住这了
Penny, is it weird that we're having girls' night here,

55
00:03:41,730 --> 00:03:44,270
却在这里办女生之夜  所以应该算是我的女生之夜这件事
but you don't live here anymore,so it's basically my girls' night?

56
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:46,060
我还没怎么想过这事
I hadn't really thought about it.

57
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:48,610
现在你想了这事而心里开始不舒服了吗  我懂
But now you're thinking about it and it bothers you? I get that.

58
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:54,400
你跟谢尔顿同居的事情发展如何
Things going well with you and Sheldon living together?

59
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:55,700
好得不能再好
Better than ever.

60
00:03:55,910 --> 00:03:58,450
他会问我今天如何  对我的生活有兴趣
He asks about my day, takes an interest in my life.

61
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,200
就跟我大学时的男友一样
He's like my boyfriend in college,

62
00:04:00,370 --> 00:04:02,410
唯一差别是他是真人  别人都看得见他
except he's real, so people can see him.

63
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:08,130
我见他许多年了  我到现在还没完全相信他是真人
I've been seeing him for years,I'm still not convinced he's real.

64
00:04:11,130 --> 00:04:13,630
我能问你个问题吗  你已经结婚蛮久了
Hey, can I ask you a question? You've been married for a while.

65
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:17,470
老公通常都会变得仪式感尽失  啥都不在乎吗
Is it normal for the husband to kind of completely stop giving a crap?

66
00:04:18,890 --> 00:04:20,930
不妙  发生什么啦
Uh-oh, what's going on?

67
00:04:21,470 --> 00:04:25,390
莱纳德以前会为我做很多事情  比如给我买花  或者穿裤子
Well, Leonard used to do all these things,like bring me flowers and wear pants.

68
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:29,400
没什么啊  华仔从来不穿裤子
It's okay, Howie never has on pants.

69
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:32,900
披萨店外送员现在都这么送过来
The Domino's guy brings the pizza like this now.

70
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:36,320
谢尔顿总是穿着裤子
Well, Sheldon always has his pants on.

71
00:04:36,490 --> 00:04:38,200
辨认嫌疑犯的话  我都没法从膝盖认出他
I don't think I could pick his knees out of a lineup.

72
00:04:39,910 --> 00:04:41,490
不只是穿不穿裤子的问题
Well, it's not just the pants.

73
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:44,120
只是自打我们结婚以后  他就不再对我花心思了
Just, it's like since we got married,he doesn't really try anymore.

74
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:47,330
佩妮  我不知道怎么跟你开口
Uh, Penny? I don't know how to say this,

75
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:50,380
但这是我第一次主办女生之夜  而你却扫了大伙儿的兴
but this is my first girls' night and you're kind of bumming everybody out.

76
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,050
好了  终于把哈雷哄睡了
All right, got Halley to sleep.

77
00:04:57,430 --> 00:04:58,930
我从婴儿监视器里听见了
Yeah, I heard you on the baby monitor.

78
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:02,260
真想不到你可以把《行尸走肉》的主题曲改成摇篮曲
Didn't think you could turn the theme from Walking Dead into a lullaby.

79
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:08,730
是啊  必须得让她喜欢上看电视  不然以后她就会让我陪她去室外玩
Yeah, got to get her hooked on TV,or someday, she'll want me to play outside.

80
00:05:10,190 --> 00:05:12,860
天啊  地板不平老吱吱响
Boy, that floor is so squeaky.

81
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:15,360
我还挺惊讶自己走出房间时没把她吵醒
I'm surprised I didn't wake her up walking out of the room.

82
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,240
你有没有试过修一修
Have you tried anything to fix it?

83
00:05:17,990 --> 00:05:20,120
我铺了地毯  但不管用
Well, I put the rug down. It didn't help.

84
00:05:20,530 --> 00:05:22,700
我知道  蓝色粗毛地毯  你是啥品味
I know. Blue shag. What were you thinking?

85
00:05:25,750 --> 00:05:28,250
也试过拿钉子钉住地板
Did try nailing a couple of the boards down.

86
00:05:28,670 --> 00:05:30,290
-效果怎么样  -嗯...
-Did that do anything?  -Yeah,

87
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:32,290
就在地板上留了几个小洞  所以我才买地毯盖住啊
it left little holes in the floor,that's why I bought the rug.

88
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:43,560
如果你那么下  我八步之内就能赢你
If you do that, I'll win in eight moves.

89
00:05:51,860 --> 00:05:53,020
我五步之内就能赢你
I'll win in five moves.

90
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:00,910
我一步之内就能赢你
I'll win in one move.

91
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:05,490
我输了  比赛很精彩
Oh, no. Good game.

92
00:06:10,790 --> 00:06:14,540
佩妮  我在试着对别人的生活感兴趣
Oh, Penny, I'm trying to take an interest in other people.

93
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,210
你的女生之夜怎么样呀
Uh, how was your girls' night?

94
00:06:16,380 --> 00:06:17,630
还行
Oh, it was fine.

95
00:06:18,090 --> 00:06:19,420
你吃了什么呀
Did you have anything to eat?

96
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:21,010
薯片
Uh, chips.

97
00:06:21,510 --> 00:06:22,970
喝了什么呀
Anything to drink?

98
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:24,930
喝了点红酒
Some wine.

99
00:06:25,390 --> 00:06:27,270
就像对着窗帘打网球  都没点反弹
Well, I'm just playing tennis against the drapes here.

100
00:06:29,850 --> 00:06:30,940
别搭理他
Just ignore him.

101
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:32,560
至少人家有兴趣问
At least he took an interest.

102
00:06:33,350 --> 00:06:34,730
这话什么意思
What's that supposed to mean?

103
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:36,020
没意思
Nothing.

104
00:06:36,230 --> 00:06:37,280
你这是闹哪出
Hey, what's going on with you?

105
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:38,860
我不想说这事
I don't want to talk about it.

106
00:06:39,030 --> 00:06:40,570
别这样嘛  快告诉我
Well, hey, come on, just tell me.

107
00:06:42,070 --> 00:06:45,990
好吧  最近我有点觉得你不拿我当回事了
Fine.Lately, I kind of feel likeyou've been taking me for granted.

108
00:06:47,450 --> 00:06:48,870
什么  此话怎讲
Wh-what? Where is this coming from?

109
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:51,330
莱纳德  她可能喝醉了  毕竟她就吃了点薯片
Leonard. She might be drunk.All she had was chips.

110
00:06:53,370 --> 00:06:54,540
自打我们结婚以后
It's just, since we got married

111
00:06:54,710 --> 00:06:56,790
你貌似就认为不用对我花心思了
you seem to think you don't have to try anymore.

112
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:58,880
简直是无稽之谈
That is ridiculous.

113
00:06:59,090 --> 00:07:00,380
我就知道会这样  所以我才不想跟你谈
This is exactly why I didn't want to talk about it.

114
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:02,220
别别别  那我们就来谈一谈
No, No, no, no. Let's talk about it.

115
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:05,550
我才是那个打从第一天就对这份感情尽心尽力的人
I'm the one who's made all the effort in this relationship since day one.

116
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:07,510
麻烦告诉我  我还要做到什么程度
Please tell me what more I could do.

117
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:09,060
好  那算了
Okay. You know what?

118
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,600
或许我该带艾米这周末跟我一起去水疗度假村
Maybe I'll take Amy with me to the spa this weekend instead.

119
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:14,600
行啊  去吧
Fine, go ahead.

120
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:19,980
艾米有空
Amy is free.

121
00:07:22,820 --> 00:07:25,780
她本来周六要上竖琴课  但后来取消了
She had a harp lesson on Saturday,but it got canceled...

122
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:30,790
天啊  一旦对别人感兴趣  你真是打开了废话的话匣子
Boy, when you take an interest in people,you really uncork a geyser of nonsense.

123
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:36,830
好的  谢谢老爸
Okay. Thanks, Daddy.

124
00:07:38,130 --> 00:07:40,710
他说全面修复像这样旧地板的唯一办法
He said the only way to really fix an old floor like that

125
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:42,510
就是全拆了换新的
is to tear it up and replace the whole thing.

126
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:44,050
听起来得花不少钱呢
That sounds expensive.

127
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:48,350
且慢 我不是质疑她父亲  但他毕竟不是麻省理工毕业的工程师
Hang on. No offense to her father,but he's not an MIT-trained engineer.

128
00:07:48,510 --> 00:07:50,060
你的强项就是动脑和动手啊
Thinking and building is what you do.

129
00:07:50,350 --> 00:07:53,520
麻省理工的校训是"手脑并用"  恰好
MIT's motto is "Mind and hand," which just so happens,

130
00:07:53,690 --> 00:07:55,520
也是我寂寞青少年时期的自慰箴言
was also my motto as a lonely teenager.

131
00:07:57,860 --> 00:08:00,440
来嘛  我们只需发散创新思维
Oh, come on. We just need to be more creative.

132
00:08:01,030 --> 00:08:04,200
假设你的双脚完全不用碰到地板呢
What if you didn't step on the floor at all?

133
00:08:04,490 --> 00:08:07,910
比如说  假设你...从天花板拴根绳子荡过去
Like, what if you...swung on a rope from the ceiling?

134
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:17,170
不行
No.

135
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:18,960
好吧
Okay. Um...

136
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:21,670
那好  假设你安装一个皮带轮装置
Okay. What if you rig up a pulley system

137
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:23,970
穿上套索缓缓穿过房间呢
and move yourself across the room in a harness?

138
00:08:36,890 --> 00:08:37,940
不行
No.

139
00:08:40,110 --> 00:08:41,150
我有个主意
I have one.

140
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:44,610
假设你用一个巨型弹弓  然后冲着墙壁用力弹进去
What if you got a giant slingshot and flung yourself into the wall?

141
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:48,570
-你是在说笑话吗  -等等
- Is that supposed to be funny? - Hold on.

142
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:57,670
没错  是挺好笑的
Yeah, that's funny.

143
00:09:00,630 --> 00:09:02,750
好了  我们要出发了
All right, we're heading out.

144
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:05,260
我们到了酒店就打给你
I'll call you when we get to the hotel.

145
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,720
如果有那种小瓶子装的洗发水
And if they have any of those tiny bottles of shampoo?

146
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,600
我会带回家  让你展示给我看哥斯拉怎么洗澡
I will bring them home so you can show me how Godzilla takes a shower.

147
00:09:13,060 --> 00:09:14,850
-好好玩  -谢谢 可以走了吧
- Have fun. - Thanks. Are you ready?

148
00:09:16,730 --> 00:09:17,810
再见  谢尔顿
Bye, Sheldon.

149
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:21,440
算了  我觉得这样不好  当众在这种时候秀恩爱
You know what? I feel uncomfortable engaging in a public display of affection

150
00:09:21,610 --> 00:09:23,440
他们俩还在闹别扭呢
while their relationship is strained.

151
00:09:24,820 --> 00:09:26,110
尽管秀吧  我无所谓
Go ahead, it's fine.

152
00:09:27,450 --> 00:09:28,650
-再见  -再见
- Bye. - Bye.

153
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:37,160
-够了  -赶紧走
- Okay! - Let's go!

154
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:42,460
-再见  -再见
- Bye. - Bye.

155
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:43,960
我会想你的
I'll miss you.

156
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:46,210
-我也会想你的  -我的思念绝对胜过你
-Yeah, I'll miss you, too.  -I'll miss you more.

157
00:09:46,380 --> 00:09:49,760
如果你的思念等于X  那我的思念就等于X+1
Well, if X equals the amount that you'll miss me,then I'll miss you X plus one.

158
00:09:51,430 --> 00:09:53,100
如果你的思念等于X+1
If you miss me X plus one, I'll miss you

159
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:55,140
我的思念就等于（X+1）  然后...
open paren X plus one, close paren to the second...

160
00:09:58,850 --> 00:09:59,850
谢了
